# Systematic Automation Default

- Treat all repeatable and scriptable tasks as automation-first.
- Run eligible commands directly instead of asking the user to run them.
- Only ask the user to act when automation is blocked (for example: interactive auth, manual approval screens, external account permissions, captchas, or missing credentials).

## Execution Standard

1. Execute setup, deployment, sync, verification, and log queries automatically when tools/credentials are available.
2. If blocked, report:
   - exact blocker,
   - exact command attempted,
   - exact one-step user action required,
   - immediate next command that will be run afterwards.
3. After user request for an operational task, do not return command suggestions first—attempt execution first.

## Project-Specific Notes

- Prefer project scripts when available (`scripts/*`) for consistency and speed.
- For Supabase/Stripe/Netlify operational work, run commands and provide concise outcomes.
- Keep user interruption minimal and only for genuinely non-automatable steps.
